            <ArticleTitle>In situ characterization of advanced glycation end products (AGEs) in collagen and model extracellular matrix by solid state NMR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13316-13319</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06624d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Non-enzymatic glycation of extracellular matrix with (U-13C5)-d-ribose-5-phosphate (R5P), enables in situ 2D ssNMR identification of many deleterious protein modifications and crosslinks, including previously unreported oxalamido and hemiaminal (CH3-CH(OH)NHR) substructures. Changes in charged residue proportions and distribution may be as important as crosslinking in provoking and understanding harmful tissue changes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
